## Phase 3 Add-On: Soft Power Off Latch Hardware (Encoder Long-Press Shutdown)

Use this section when replacing the external slide switch with the encoder push + firmware-controlled soft power latch.

### Core parts (required)

| Qty | Part Number | Description | Unit Price | DigiKey Link |
|-----|------------|-------------|-----------|-------------|
| 1 | BS250P | P-channel MOSFET, TO-92 through-hole, high-side load switch element | ~$0.50 | [Link](https://www.digikey.com/en/products/detail/diodes-incorporated/BS250P/92630) |
| 1 | 2N3904 | NPN transistor (latch control / gate pull-down driver) | ~$0.10 | [Link](https://www.digikey.com/en/products/detail/diotec-semiconductor/2N3904/13164701) |
| 1 | CF14JT100K | 100 kOhm 1/4W resistor (PMOS gate pull-up to source, default OFF) | ~$0.10 | [Link](https://www.digikey.com/en/products/detail/stackpole-electronics-inc/CF14JT100K/1741263) |
| 1 | CF14JT1K00 | 1 kOhm 1/4W resistor (MCU HOLD or base-drive series resistor) | ~$0.10 | [Link](https://www.digikey.com/en/products/detail/stackpole-electronics-inc/CF14JT1K00/1741314) |
| 1 | 1N4148 | Small signal diode, DO-35 (optional but recommended for steering/OR paths in latch variants) | ~$0.10 | [Link](https://www.digikey.com/en/products/detail/onsemi/1N4148/458603) |

### Reused existing BOM parts in the latch block

- Reuse existing 100 nF ceramic part K104K15X7RF5TL2 for optional RC timing/debounce node(s).
- Reuse existing CF14JT10K0 where a 10 kOhm bias resistor is needed by your chosen latch topology.

### Wiring intent summary for this BOM section

- SYS_IN (from charger OUT+) -> PMOS source.
- VSYS (switched rail) -> PMOS drain -> regulator VIN.
- PMOS gate pulled high to source by 100 kOhm (default OFF).
- NPN transistor pulls PMOS gate low to turn ON when button pulse or MCU HOLD requests ON.
- Encoder push is dual use: short press for UI mode change, long press firmware shutdown, then MCU drops HOLD.

### Build note

BS250P is through-hole and aligns with your all-through-hole assembly preference.

